First, let me understand the problem clearly:

- We have `demand` array for cars in order (car 0, car 1, ..., car n-1)
- Two dispensers with initial fuel amounts `fuel[0]` and `fuel[1]`
- Cars become allowed at times: car 0 at time 0, car i at time equal to when car i-1 starts refueling
- When a car becomes allowed, we must choose a dispenser with at least `demand[i]` fuel remaining
- Car starts refueling immediately when the chosen dispenser becomes free (if it's already free, waiting time = 0; otherwise, waiting time = time until dispenser becomes free)
- We need to maximize the number of served cars first, then minimize the maximum waiting time among all served cars
- Return -1 if no car can be served

